″}+144y=0,\n$$\n\nwhere $t>0$ is the time, in seconds. What is the period of the oscillation?" :question/worked-solution "The simple harmonic motion (SHM) equation is\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}+{\\omega }^{2}y=0.\n$$\n\nIn our case\n\n$$\n{\\omega }^{2}=144\\,⟹\\,\\omega =12.\n$$\n\nThe period $T$ is given by:\n\n$$\nT=\\frac{2\\pi }{\\omega }\n$$\n\nTherefore, in our case, the period (in seconds) is\n\n$$\nT=\\frac{2\\pi }{12}=\\frac{\\pi }{6}\\,\\text{s}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-94274/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "ef654722-031d-51cc-86fc-a0cbc498b350"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-94274"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-64250/selection/a690dcfd520d09d276d2ba9ed3722b8071bc5f5804cf35b34d123ef2db600227" :answer/id #uuid "1f84a930-159c-5339-8a5c-fe78024c9cbb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{4}\\,\\text{s}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-64250/selection/c52fa96f46dc62b1281c92c37627774fac8b92062bf7f987f12de62459a56846" :answer/id #uuid "e88ecc89-2f48-5c5b-aa99-9f0cf6a47b4a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2\\pi \\,\\text{s}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-64250/selection/55c3723a2e8731ecab6008eb93d2495c972f34450512e7c59f06338980c95232" :answer/id #uuid "9792f5e8-b49a-5d7a-9639-f4e8d2427744" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4\\pi \\,\\text{s}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-64250/selection/3e311265a6bcd67f92fccbb5db03f7bbbf0b2a6e30b3d18363d2686e030dbf15" :answer/id #uuid "33948804-9e48-5bc6-af8f-096f64aced2c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\pi \\,\\text{s}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-64250/selection/fa390f0fe3bdefe27437e709b214a7a294db52a9b1efe1868e91488b62415aa9" :answer/id #uuid "3b62f36e-9be6-5ddc-bca7-b24af9d8799b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{2}\\,\\text{s}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-64250