is the time, in seconds. What is the period of the oscillation?" :question/worked-solution "The simple harmonic motion (SHM) equation is\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}+{\\omega }^{2}y=0.\n$$\n\nIn our case\n\n$$\n{\\omega }^{2}=2\\,⟹\\,\\omega =\\sqrt{2}.\n$$\n\nThe period $T$ is given by:\n\n$$\nT=\\frac{2\\pi }{\\omega }\n$$\n\nTherefore, in our case, the period (in seconds) is\n\n$$\nT=\\frac{2\\pi }{\\sqrt{2}}=\\sqrt{2}\\pi \\,\\text{s}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-94271/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "ef654722-031d-51cc-86fc-a0cbc498b350"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-94271"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-79487/selection/1f1f2fe9df6485d5cdc7916416b2f79699d874348406e639d5daec02cb2e57e6" :answer/id #uuid "fe253760-a70f-52a1-b564-9847905ca0a3" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-79487/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" :answer/id #uuid "1c30f992-6426-5748-b05a-d18cd90a9c6c" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-79487/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" :answer/id #uuid "f12927cc-8327-5864-9f60-0d40fcd56a7d" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-79487/selection/431472f1dab61ef54de031c09a96fb6a21dc69c8bc09f12797d1d686e8c9e8e6" :answer/id #uuid "0ba3b544-cdf6-597b-88a6-a39ad5688374" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-79487/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" :answer/id #uuid "a60c204b-670b-52ee-bbf9-36c00385a5b3" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-79487/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "2f502ef3-516a-59f2-9e5f-2d7b226570ca" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-79487/selection/431472f1dab61ef54de031c09a96fb6a21dc69c8bc09f12797d1d686e8c9e8e6" :answer-field/choices ["q-79487/selection/1f1f2fe9df6485d5cdc7916416b2f79699d874348406e639d5daec02cb2e57e6" "q-79487/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" "q-79487/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" "q-79487/selection/431472f1dab61ef54de031c09a96fb6a21dc69c8bc09f12797d1d686e8c9e8e6" "q-79487/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-79487" :question/id #uuid "66fc565d-c8ed-53ce-9b96-5834b31ff064" :question/math-academy-id "q-79487" :question/problem "A particle is moving with simple harmonic motion. The position of the particle $y(t)$ at time $t$ is governed by the equation\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}+2y=0.\n$$\n\nWhich of the following could be used to represent the general solution for $y(t)?$\n\n- $y=R\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\sqrt{2}t+{ϕ}_{1})$\n- $y=R\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t+{ϕ}_{2})$\n- $y=A\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\sqrt{2}t+B\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\sqrt{2}t$\n\nNote that $R,{ϕ}_{1},{ϕ}_{2},A$ and $B$ are constants." :question/worked-solution "The SHM equation is\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}+{\\omega }^{2}y=0.\n$$\n\nThe general solution to the SHM equation can be written in three different forms:\n\n- $y=R\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\omega t+{ϕ}_{1})$\n\n- $y=R\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\omega t+{ϕ}_{2})$\n\n- $y=A\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\omega t+B\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\omega t$\n\nIn our case\n\n$$\n{\\omega }^{2}=2\\,⟹\\,\\omega =\\sqrt{2}.\n$$\n\nThus, we have:\n\n- $y=R\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\sqrt{2}t+{ϕ}_{1})$\n\n- $y=R\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\sqrt{2}t+{ϕ}_{2})$\n\n- $y=A\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\sqrt{2}t+B\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\sqrt{2}t$\n\nTherefore, only functions I and III could be used to represent $y(t).$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-79487/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "e17fe7fc-3b85-5f2c-aa69-2336b05b16b2"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-79487"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-94278/selection/431472f1dab61ef54de031c09a96fb6a21dc69c8bc09f12797d1d686e8c9e8e6" :answer/id #uuid "47171b38-b4e2-53b9-bc7a-23ff02cfed31" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-94278/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" :answer/id #uuid "2c1db7b9-c51c-5d9b-a5b7-8359165afc04" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-94278/selection/1f1f2fe9df6485d5cdc7916416b2f79699d874348406e639d5daec02cb2e57e6" :answer/id #uuid "1bade982-7efa-54e0-bf4f-7fd8556f41e7" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-94278/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" :answer/id #uuid "053a87b2-696a-52e1-b793-fb646d50d388" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-94278/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" :answer/id #uuid "0c12f5e9-90fb-5c47-a7a5-ae27a7ec95b1" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-94278/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "72053b29-dbc5-5281-8acf-bd9ae7fd08a9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-94278/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" :answer-field/choices ["q-94278/selection/431472f1dab61ef54de031c09a96fb6a21dc69c8bc09f12797d1d686e8c9e8e6" "q-94278/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" "q-94278/selection/1f1f2fe9df6485d5cdc7916416b2f79699d874348406e639d5daec02cb2e57e6" "q-94278/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" "q-94278/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-94278" :question/id #uuid "23f8b8a5-7c24-563a-a40e-d60abf329c96" :question/math-academy-id "q-94278" :question/problem "A particle is moving with simple harmonic motion. The position of the particle $y(t)$ at time $t$ is governed by the equation\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}+5y=0.\n$$\n\nWhich of the following could be used to represent the general solution for $y(t)?$\n\n- $y=R\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5t+{ϕ}_{1})$\n- $y=R\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\sqrt{5}t+{ϕ}_{2})$\n- $y=A\\operatorname{sec}⁡\\sqrt{5}t+B\\operatorname{csc}⁡\\sqrt{5}t$\n\nNote that $R,{ϕ}_{1},{ϕ}_{2},A$ and $B$ are constants." :question/worked-solution "The SHM equation is\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}+{\\omega }^{2}y=0.\n$$\n\nThe general solution to the SHM equation can be written in three different forms:\n\n- $y=R\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\omega t+{ϕ}_{1})$\n\n- $y=R\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\omega t+{ϕ}_{2})$\n\n- $y=A\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\omega t+B\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\omega t$\n\nIn our case\n\n$$\n{\\omega }^{2}=5\\,⟹\\,\\omega =\\sqrt{5}.\n$$\n\nThus, we have:\n\n- $y=R\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\sqrt{5}t+{ϕ}_{1})$\n\n- $y=R\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\sqrt{5}t+{ϕ}_{2})$\n\n- $y=A\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\sqrt{5}t+B\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\sqrt{5}t$\n\nTherefore, only statement II could be used to represent $y(t).$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-94278/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "e17fe7fc-3b85-5f2c-aa69-2336b05b16b2"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-94278"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-64252/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" :answer/id #uuid "300647d7-9ca6-5331-a12f-c7402de2fb3b" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-64252/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc5